> 
> 
> Returning data from database is hardly a streaming use case to be honest, databases don't stream results (in the `Multi` fashion). In almost all cases, returning `Uni<List<Whateve>>` is the proper way to handle the database results.
> 
> In any case, can you show some pseudocode of what you have in mind?

Not a database streaming example, but hopefully it shows my point.

```kotlin
    @GET
    @Path("/1")
    @Produces(MediaType.TEXT_PLAIN)
    suspend fun parse(
        file: FileUpload
    ): Flow<String> {
        readOrWriteSomethingFromOrToTheDatabase()
        return parseCsvFile(file.uploadedFile())
    }

    private suspend fun readOrWriteSomethingFromOrToTheDatabase() {
        // database access (or any other dependent function) needs a suspendable function
        // In our applications we us suspendable function heavilly.
    }

    private fun parseCsvFile(path: java.nio.file.Path): Flow<String> {
        return path.bufferedReader()
            .lines()
            .consumeAsFlow()
            .map { it.uppercase() }
            .flowOn(Dispatchers.IO) // Dispatchers.IO used here only as an example
    }
```
